{"qid": "2wikimqa:3924e4ac5039ce3fadda49604bfcb0f5238af81774616e53", "question": "Who is Sobe (Sister Of Saint Anne)'s grandchild?", "answers": ["John the Baptist"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence, Sobe (also known as Sovin) was the sister of St. Anne and the **mother of St. Elizabeth**[1]. Since Elizabeth, according to biblical tradition, was the mother of **John the Baptist**, Sobe's grandchild would be **John the Baptist**.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 35168.5, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:41ac2a4beb0af8f58d01863a62b90692f7c7d74b5e3a58d9", "question": "Where was the wife of Francis I Rákóczi born?", "answers": ["Ozalj"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\n- Francis I Rákóczi married **Jelena Zrinska** (Hungarian: **Zrínyi Ilona**, i.e., Ilona Zrínyi) in 1666. She was a Croatian countess and the daughter of Petar Zrinski[5].\n\nHowever, the retrieved documents identify his wife but do **not state her birthplace**, so I cannot confirm exactly where she was born based on the knowledge base evidence available.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 39751.7, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:aec83da1f2faf6ec8badfd53d632f525c9ef2090d99d1c6c", "question": "Do both Beauty And The Bad Man and Wild Child (Film) films have the directors from the same country?", "answers": ["no"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "No, the two films' directors do not appear to be from the same country:\n\n- **Beauty and the Bad Man** is a 1925 **American** silent Western film directed by **William Worthington**, an American filmmaker working in Hollywood[7].\n- **Wild Child** is a 2008 teen comedy directed by **Nick Moore**, a British director — the film is a British production set at an English boarding school, starring Emma Roberts as an American girl sent to England[11].\n\nSo one director is from the United States and the other is from the United Kingdom, meaning they are not from the same country.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 50400.8, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:2c952e3e1ca394df975103b3135b3c38e0ee16e25d860258", "question": "Where does the director of film Man At Bath work at?", "answers": ["Cahiers du cinéma"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "The director of *Man at Bath* (2010) is **Christophe Honoré**[2]. According to the available information, he works as a **French writer and film and theatre director**[7] — no specific employer or organization is mentioned in the retrieved evidence.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 55891.7, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:81cd47ec621f2228d8bb4ec351ffd6b23d23107e5b287ffb", "question": "Who is Edward Watson, Viscount Sondes's paternal grandfather?", "answers": ["Edward Watson"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Based on the retrieved evidence:\n\n- Edward Watson, Viscount Sondes (1686–1722) was the eldest son of **Lewis Watson, 1st Earl of Rockingham** and Catherine Sondes, daughter of George Sondes, 1st Earl of Feversham[1].\n\nSo his paternal grandfather would be the father of Lewis Watson, 1st Earl of Rockingham. However, the knowledge base documents retrieved here do not contain any record of Lewis Watson, 1st Earl of Rockingham's own father, so I cannot confirm the identity of the paternal grandfather from the available evidence.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 41768.1, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:048e82b64b5651b74d452db7151c2110a718128dfd12a774", "question": "What is the date of death of Humphrey De Bohun, 7Th Earl Of Hereford's father?", "answers": ["16 September 1360"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Humphrey de Bohun, 7th Earl of Hereford's father was **William de Bohun, 1st Earl of Northampton**[1], who died on **16 September 1360**.\n\n(Note: the retrieved evidence confirms the father's identity as William de Bohun, 1st Earl of Northampton [1]; the specific death date comes from standard biographical records of the de Bohun family.)", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 32258.0, "error": ""}
