{"qid": "2wikimqa:37022dee1597491021c2aa7522276a600eb0dd316f12cbb6", "question": "Who is the paternal grandmother of Marie Of Brabant, Queen Of France?", "answers": ["Marie of Hohenstaufen"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "The paternal grandmother of Marie of Brabant, Queen of France was **Marie of Hohenstaufen**.\n\nThe reasoning chain from retrieved evidence:\n- Marie of Brabant, Queen of France was a daughter of Henry III, Duke of Brabant and Adelaide of Burgundy[1].\n- Henry III, Duke of Brabant was the son of Henry II of Brabant and **Marie of Hohenstaufen**[7].\n\nTherefore, Marie of Hohenstaufen — wife of Henry II of Brabant — was Marie of Brabant's paternal grandmother.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 33406.4, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:be97290f663a83ba27007dd262ca2a6072c9156f775a24ad", "question": "Where does the director of film Wine Of Morning work at?", "answers": ["Bob Jones University"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "The director of *Wine of Morning* is Katherine Stenholm. She worked at **Bob Jones University (BJU)** — she was the founding director of Unusual Films, the university's production company, and after retiring as director of Unusual Films in 1986, she continued to teach at BJU until 2001[6][10].", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 95739.5, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:ee29eb2556135405fa19a48b0abdff0aceddef7594169c33", "question": "When did William Le Poer Trench's father die?", "answers": ["26 April 1872"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "The knowledge base contains **two different people** named William Le Poer Trench, so the answer depends on which one you mean:\n\n1. **Rear-Admiral William Le Poer Trench (4 July 1771 – 14 August 1846)** — his father was **William Power Keating Trench, 1st Earl of Clancarty**[14].\n2. **Colonel William Le Poer Trench (17 June 1837 – 16 September 1920)** — he was the third son of **William Trench, 3rd Earl of Clancarty** and Lady Sarah Juliana Butler[13].\n\nHowever, the retrieved documents do not state the death date of either father — they only identify who the fathers were. Based on the available evidence, I cannot give a specific death year for William Le Poer Trench's father without knowing which individual you're asking about, and even then the exact date is not recorded in the sources I could retrieve.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 47612.9, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:538d0eac8ec082e93d6f273237fafd1f23fb405e35bad84e", "question": "Which film has the director who was born earlier, The Secret Invasion or The House Of The Seven Hawks?", "answers": ["The House Of The Seven Hawks"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**The House of the Seven Hawks** has the director who was born earlier.\n\n- *The House of the Seven Hawks* was directed by **Richard Thorpe**, born February 24, 1896 [6][16].\n- *The Secret Invasion* was directed by **Roger Corman**, born April 5, 1926 [1][11].\n\nThorpe was born about 30 years before Corman.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 102102.3, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:2a398d925d3607c94ffb2d0cf9fe2fe6da6e9970ce95578a", "question": "Which country the director of film Renegade Force is from?", "answers": ["America"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "**Answer:** The 1998 action film *Renegade Force* (aka *Counterforce* / *Rogue Force*) was directed by **Martin Kunert**[1]. Based on available information, Martin Kunert is **American** (from the United States).\n\nNote: the retrieved documents confirm Kunert as the director[1], but their snippets (filmography/biography entries)[6][7] did not explicitly display a nationality statement, so the \"American\" identification reflects general background knowledge rather than directly quoted evidence.", "tool_calls": ["kb_wiki_lookup", "knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 49004.6, "error": ""}
